Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.82,0:00:07.07,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Tell me something, Nanase.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.53,0:00:13.73,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Tsukishiro said he'd sent a student \Nfrom the White Room as an assassin.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.04,0:00:15.79,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Was that all a bluff?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.46,0:00:19.12,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,I don't know what that means.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.36,0:00:25.00,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,I don't know much about \Nthe White Room myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.52,0:00:28.29,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,She doesn't appear to be lying.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.29,0:00:32.72,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,And she's not competent enough \Nto be the assassin herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.56,0:00:35.08,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Which means...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.00,0:00:40.16,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Looks like we're in for \Na real downpour, huh,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.72,0:00:43.02,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Senpai?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.57,0:00:58.37,S4_Show_Title,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(1800,0)}Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.45,0:02:09.00,S4_Show_Title,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(450,0)}Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.70,0:02:18.11,S4_Ep_Title,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(800,550)\an2\pos(320,310)}#13 Obscured By the Rain
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.99,0:02:18.49,Main_Top,Nanase,0,0,0,,Get behind me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.49,0:02:19.68,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.68,0:02:23.00,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Nanase-chan, you're not happy to see me?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.00,0:02:26.74,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,What an awful way to treat \Nyour own groupmate...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.74,0:02:31.76,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Or did this little guy here \Nmake me look threatening?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.76,0:02:33.76,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,I can't trust you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.76,0:02:35.76,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Not nice!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.36,0:02:38.56,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Why would you even say that?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.56,0:02:40.64,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,I'm such a li'l cutie pie!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.64,0:02:44.48,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Seriously, I'm not a bad girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.48,0:02:46.64,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Right, Ayanokoji-senpai?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.02,0:02:49.40,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Let's talk a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.62,0:02:53.26,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,Senpai, there's something \NI haven't told you about.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.40,0:02:57.85,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,After the rest of you went \Nlooking for Shinohara-senpai,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.85,0:03:02.79,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,I sensed someone watching us \Nand chased after them.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.08,0:03:06.08,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,They ran, so I was unable \Nto catch up with them,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.40,0:03:08.79,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,but they had a distinct hairstyle.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.79,0:03:10.29,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,Amasawa-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.65,0:03:13.55,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,You hurt Komiya-senpai and \NKinoshita-senpai, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.05,0:03:18.23,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Let me turn that one around on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.23,0:03:21.87,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,If it turned out I {\i1}did{\i0} do it...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.87,0:03:23.56,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,What would you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.85,0:03:25.62,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,I'd want to know why you did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.06,0:03:32.07,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,More importantly... why didn't your \Nname show up on the GPS tracker?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.07,0:03:35.55,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Erasing your presence isn't \Ndifficult in and of itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.90,0:03:38.45,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,You just have to damage your watch.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.45,0:03:42.06,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,You heard him, Nanase-chan.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.58,0:03:45.65,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Why have you come here?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.65,0:03:49.32,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Or rather... how exactly did you find us?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.32,0:03:52.92,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Slow down now, Ayanokoji-senpai.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.92,0:03:55.84,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Let's savor the fact that \Nwe found each other at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.15,0:04:00.09,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, but I'd like to keep \Nthis brief, given the rain and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.31,0:04:04.82,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Then how about we have a \Nsleepover chat in your tent?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.85,0:04:07.83,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Hands-on contact, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.83,0:04:11.98,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,I want to talk to Ayanokoji-senpai. \NStep aside, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.98,0:04:14.32,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,You can talk right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.32,0:04:16.61,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,No, I don't think we can.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.61,0:04:21.13,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,We'll be talking about \Nthe White Room, see?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.68,0:04:25.74,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,You get it now, little Miss Outsider?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.67,0:04:30.50,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Sorry,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.73,0:04:34.90,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,but I won't believe you're from the \NWhite Room just because you know about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.40,0:04:38.35,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,What would you gain from \Nrevealing your identity?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.35,0:04:40.04,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,What do I gain?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.04,0:04:44.89,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,I wanted to let you know \Nthat I'm not your enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.13,0:04:46.77,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,That doesn't add up.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.13,0:04:52.15,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,The White Room student is an assassin \Nsent here to get me expelled.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.42,0:04:55.26,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,To say that you're not my enemy \Nisn't logically consistent.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.58,0:04:57.85,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,I'm sure he thought a White Room student
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.85,0:05:02.41,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,would happily expel you out of jealousy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.63,0:05:06.32,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,But he didn't anticipate that I'd be a
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.32,0:05:11.29,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,pure-hearted young maiden bursting \Nwith admiration for you!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.53,0:05:17.17,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Then why didn't you reveal all this the \Nmoment you arrived at the school?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.17,0:05:24.54,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Because, as much as I admired you, \NI'd never actually met you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.54,0:05:29.68,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,I needed time to watch you and see if \Nthat "Oh, I'm so glad I admired him!"
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.03,0:05:33.19,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,reaction was in the cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.59,0:05:36.41,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,If you had the same upbringing I did,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.41,0:05:39.94,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I suppose you've realized how \Ninteresting this school is, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.30,0:05:45.79,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Yeah, I've thought plenty about \Nhow much I'd love to stay here and
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.79,0:05:47.92,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,enjoy myself until graduation.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.38,0:05:53.58,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Though I'm awful at making friends, \Nso I don't have many people to talk to.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.80,0:06:00.46,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,But I'm not totally lacking in \Ncommunication skills like you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.96,0:06:05.01,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,There are things only the fifth class, \None year below yours, is learning:
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.71,0:06:10.67,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,the ability to hold a basic conversation.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.67,0:06:14.56,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,As a member of the fourth class, \Nyou're surely aware that its focus
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.56,0:06:18.11,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,on pure individualism crushed \Nnearly everyone in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.11,0:06:20.19,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I believe your story now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.62,0:06:25.24,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,But I don't feel you've adequately \Nexplained why you've revealed yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.48,0:06:28.86,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,You seem pretty calm for \Nsomeone who just accepted
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.86,0:06:30.66,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,that I'm a White Room student.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.99,0:06:35.00,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Maybe you think I can't \Nbe a threat to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.63,0:06:40.05,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Oh, well... I've told \Nyou what I wanted to,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.05,0:06:42.13,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,so I think I'll be on my way.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.94,0:06:49.74,Main,Amasawa,0,0,0,,Don't go getting crushed without \Nmy permission, all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.62,0:06:57.04,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.48,0:06:59.73,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,Senpai?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.23,0:07:05.76,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,Are those Amasawa-san's tracks?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.76,0:07:10.74,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Yes. There were tracks nearby when \NKomiya and Kinoshita were injured.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.09,0:07:14.62,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,The size is about the same as \NAmasawa's, so I can be certain.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.94,0:07:19.78,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Amasawa seems to have \Napproached me from behind...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.63,0:07:27.26,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,But when the tracks get closer \Nto us, they become scrambled.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.19,0:07:33.10,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,And then the set of mystery tracks \Nturns back for some reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.34,0:07:40.46,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,Someone else was here before \NAmasawa-san called out to us, you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.46,0:07:47.86,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Yes. And this stick has been \Ntrimmed for use as a weapon.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.26,0:07:53.32,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,If Amasawa had wanted to attack me, \Nshe should have ambushed me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.76,0:07:57.50,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,However, she showed no sign of hostility.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.80,0:08:03.85,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,So it wasn't Amasawa-san who brought this \Nstick, but whoever made these tracks?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.47,0:08:06.51,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,But why...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.51,0:08:10.89,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Amasawa said she admired me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.21,0:08:16.62,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,If she thought I was about to \Nbe attacked, it makes sense that
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.62,0:08:18.16,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,she would protect me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.16,0:08:23.82,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,Declaring her an ally based on \Nonly that feels dangerous to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.09,0:08:26.08,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Either way, the situation is what it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.56,0:08:28.86,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Let's set up the tents quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.33,0:08:42.96,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\an7\fs12\shad0\3c&H9599A8&}Advanced Nurturing High School Management\NDue to today's suspension of testing due to poor weather,\Nonly 1/4 of movement and challenge tasks were able\Nto be completed. The final day's arrival bonuses,\Narrival order rewards, and challenge rewards will all be\Ndoubled to compensate for this loss in points.\NThe weather is expected to improve tomorrow morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.69,0:08:36.08,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,"To make up for the suspension of the test,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.08,0:08:39.56,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,all rewards on the last \Nday will be doubled."
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.92,0:08:42.96,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,That could result in dramatic comebacks.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.37,0:08:48.29,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,They've also given us time to consider \Nhow to plan for the late game.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.92,0:08:50.01,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,Senpai.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.16,0:08:53.60,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Nanase?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.82,0:08:57.38,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,I want to talk to you. May I come in?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.54,0:09:01.85,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,So? What did you want to \Ntalk about in the rain?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.60,0:09:07.53,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,I was certain that Amasawa-san \Nhad pushed those two students,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.53,0:09:10.99,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,but you don't seem to \Nthink that's a guarantee.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.27,0:09:16.18,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,There's no way to confirm if \NAmasawa did anything to them,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.18,0:09:19.63,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,but I've more or less figured \Nout who's on what table.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.10,0:09:24.56,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,On the sixth day, when GPS search \Nrestrictions were lifted,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.56,0:09:26.75,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I conducted ten such searches.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.40,0:09:32.02,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It's an extremely useful tool to \Nlearn where other students are.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.02,0:09:34.23,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,I'm sorry if this is a rude question,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.23,0:09:37.51,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,but was that really worth \Nspending ten game points on?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.51,0:09:41.83,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Each GPS search does cost \None game point, true,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.83,0:09:44.77,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,and a single usage is far from effective.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.77,0:09:50.05,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,However, repeated searches \Nallowed me to connect the dots
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.05,0:09:52.68,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,and see patterns I hadn't noticed before.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.04,0:09:56.34,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,For instance, there are a \Nnumber of third-year groups
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.34,0:10:00.54,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,that are always sticking close to \Nthe Nagumo and Kiriyama groups.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.91,0:09:55.24,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,175)\pos(255.333,227.333)\fs8\3c&HCE5D60&\shad0}Nagumo G
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.16,0:09:56.87,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(125,175)\fs8\3c&HCE5D60&\shad0\pos(270,222)}Nagumo G
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.16,0:09:56.87,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(125,175)\fs8\3c&HCE5D60&\shad0\pos(290,255)}Kiriyama G
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.78,0:09:58.49,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(125,175)\fs8\3c&HCE5D60&\shad0\pos(262.667,223.333)}Nagumo G
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.78,0:09:58.49,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(125,175)\fs8\3c&HCE5D60&\shad0\pos(288.667,254.333)}Kiriyama G
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.41,0:10:00.00,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(125,175)\fs8\3c&HCE5D60&\shad0\pos(270.667,212)}Nagumo G
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.41,0:10:00.00,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(125,175)\fs8\3c&HCE5D60&\shad0\pos(300,239.667)}Kiriyama G
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.91,0:10:00.54,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(125,0)\fs8\3c&HCE5D60&\shad0\pos(283.333,192)}Nagumo G
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.91,0:10:00.54,Sign_Basic,sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(125,0)\fs8\3c&HCE5D60&\shad0\pos(314,221.667)}Kiriyama G
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.12,0:10:04.96,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,They're likely arranging things \Nin advance so that Nagumo
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.96,0:10:08.30,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,effortlessly takes first place in \Nany challenge he participates in.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.92,0:10:11.14,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,We can assume the groups \Ncooperating with Nagumo
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.14,0:10:14.11,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,are being made to compete \Namong themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.56,0:10:17.28,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Nagumo has probably also \Nprepared his own method
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.28,0:10:19.82,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,to avoid expulsion in an emergency.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.34,0:10:23.69,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,It's like the student council president \Nis holding a test of his own.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.97,0:10:27.79,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Nagumo has his entire class year \Nunder his thumb, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.79,0:10:31.07,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,As one of the people who makes the rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.49,0:10:34.92,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Of course, like Nagumo,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.92,0:10:39.20,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,a small group of second-years are taking \Na strategy of helping each other.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.50,0:10:43.49,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,But unlike Nagumo, \Nwe negotiated that as equals.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.01,0:10:47.65,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,One thing the second-year \Nleaders have going for them
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.65,0:10:50.98,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,is the ability to work together \Nwhen their interests align.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.52,0:10:55.72,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,I can see why that information was \Nworth spending ten game points for.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.11,0:11:00.41,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,The minute the rain stops, \NI'm going to go after Amasawa-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.41,0:11:03.86,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,Now that she's made it clear \Nshe's a White Room student,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.86,0:11:06.05,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,I'm worried about what she'll do next.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.39,0:11:08.68,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I wouldn't recommend that.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.68,0:11:11.86,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Focus on protecting yourself, not me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.11,0:11:14.41,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,I'm not afraid of being expelled.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.41,0:11:18.24,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,I intend to do whatever \Nit takes to protect you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.71,0:11:20.87,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Allow me to rephrase.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.87,0:11:23.35,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Having you out there \Nacting as a wild card
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.35,0:11:26.00,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,could hinder me in unexpected ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.59,0:11:29.93,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I'd like you to avoid making risky moves.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.38,0:11:33.60,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,True... I wouldn't want to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.25,0:11:37.26,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,I don't want to make any \Nmore trouble for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.63,0:11:40.85,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Besides, Hosen's in your group, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.85,0:11:44.02,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Be careful moving forward. All right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.27,0:11:46.85,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,Very well. I promise I will.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.23,0:11:53.64,Main,Nanase,0,0,0,,I suppose this is goodbye \Nfor a while, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.30,0:12:06.75,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Ayanokoji-kun?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.15,0:12:09.66,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I haven't seen you since the first day.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.30,0:12:13.50,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,You're in better shape than I expected.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.87,0:12:15.48,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Are you still on your own?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.48,0:12:19.76,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I've faced my share of adversity, \Nbut it also makes many things easier.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.01,0:12:22.63,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Did you hear about Shinohara's group?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.63,0:12:23.64,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.64,0:12:26.89,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Sakayanagi-san just \Ntold me about it today.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.89,0:12:30.23,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,So you didn't refuse her offer?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.23,0:12:32.15,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,I had no reason to do so.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.57,0:12:35.61,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Shinohara-san's group is currently \Nseventh from the bottom.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.94,0:12:40.29,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,If she can't find a group to \Njoin up with, I'll take action.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.29,0:12:44.41,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Luckily, I've managed to open three \Ngroup slots through challenge success.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.41,0:12:50.08,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,But then you and Shinohara-san will have \Nto get game points all by yourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.08,0:12:54.04,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I'd prefer to have them absorbed by \Na group with lots of game points.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.27,0:12:55.26,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.26,0:13:00.68,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Still, I've become keenly aware of the \Nnumber of groups that have transceivers.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.68,0:13:04.15,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,That does seem common among \Nthe well-organized upper classes
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.15,0:13:06.81,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,with lots of points to spend.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.26,0:13:13.06,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,Could we have done the same if \Nwe'd trusted each other a bit more?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.06,0:13:16.06,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It could also prove a waste of resources.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.06,0:13:18.82,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It won't necessarily help them.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.12,0:13:20.22,Main,Horikita,0,0,0,,True.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.30,0:13:27.13,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,My total game points \Nare just a hair behind
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.13,0:13:29.10,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,those of the tenth-place Kuronaga group.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.56,0:13:33.93,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,The important thing is to \Nstay just below tenth place.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.58,0:13:36.71,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,If I enter the top ten and stand out,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.71,0:13:39.94,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,it raises the chances of rivals \Nattempting to hinder me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.34,0:13:45.85,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I want to maintain my ideal placement \Nand get in touch with Sakayanagi soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.10,0:13:53.10,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Is anyone in there?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.86,0:13:59.69,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Sorry, but I'll be setting \Nup my tent nearby.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.69,0:14:01.61,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,If you have a problem \Nwith that, let me know.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.12,0:14:10.46,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,I was wondering what kind of \Nfreak showed up. So it was you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.62,0:14:14.43,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Was I making too much noise?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.43,0:14:15.63,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,Nah.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.58,0:14:26.80,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,May I come in?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.80,0:14:28.85,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I want to ask you something.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.98,0:14:32.02,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I'm opening up. Is that okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.82,0:14:36.61,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,What's that you're eating?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.66,0:14:38.86,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,Jerky.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.86,0:14:43.24,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Jerky? That wasn't in the \Nmanual we were given.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.24,0:14:44.99,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,So what?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.99,0:14:46.87,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,It's none of your business.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.80,0:14:52.00,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,What are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.00,0:14:54.00,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Your pulse is racing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.00,0:14:56.09,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Your lips are parched, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.09,0:14:58.22,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Clear signs of dehydration.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.96,0:15:02.51,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,I'm not thirsty... anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.51,0:15:06.24,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,"Anymore" suggests you \Nwere thirsty before.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.24,0:15:07.84,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,It's none of your business!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.24,0:15:10.43,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,I'm doing just fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.35,0:15:14.54,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,Hey! Don't you touch—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.94,0:15:16.81,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,How long have you gone without water?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.03,0:15:18.81,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,I don't have to tell you anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.81,0:15:20.44,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,How long?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.04,0:15:24.95,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,A little over a day.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.95,0:15:27.76,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,And you've been walking around like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.76,0:15:30.34,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,I can always go back to the \Nstarting point if I have to.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.34,0:15:31.33,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,Leave me alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.33,0:15:33.36,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,That's quite far from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.68,0:15:35.96,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,If you collapse on the \Nway, you're finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.96,0:15:38.83,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,Then I'll win a challenge or something!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.83,0:15:42.59,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,If it were that simple, \Nyou wouldn't be struggling now.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.29,0:15:48.44,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Let's make a trade.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.79,0:15:49.84,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.84,0:15:52.69,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I'm running low on food myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.16,0:15:55.98,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,And I have a bit more water than I need.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.43,0:16:01.95,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I think we can make a trade on even \Nterms, so I'd like to negotiate.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.22,0:16:07.42,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Well? Once again, I'm offering \Na trade on even terms.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.42,0:16:09.83,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,In exchange for this, \NI'd like some of your food.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.83,0:16:11.87,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,Hell no.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.19,0:16:13.88,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,You're free to refuse.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.88,0:16:16.00,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,But I won't make this offer again.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.50,0:16:22.88,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,If you drop out due to dehydration now, \Nyou're guaranteed to lose to Horikita.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.91,0:16:27.37,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,Fine. I accept your trade.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.37,0:16:30.39,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,But how much food do you want?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.39,0:16:34.64,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Half of the food you \Nhave left. It's a deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.66,0:16:44.65,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,You only have one left.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.65,0:16:47.16,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,This was "more water than you need"?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.16,0:16:50.16,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,Did you think I'd feel indebted \Nto you if you saved me?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.16,0:16:52.16,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,If you hadn't looked into it,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.16,0:16:55.30,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,you wouldn't have felt \Nindebted in the first place.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.05,0:17:00.04,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Even if you were indebted, \Nwould you ever try to pay it back?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.04,0:17:01.36,Main,Ibuki,0,0,0,,Hell no.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.17,0:17:03.18,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.60,0:17:22.03,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,You arrived quite late, Ayanokoji.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.67,0:17:25.90,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It does appear so.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.90,0:17:30.87,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,I was thinking I had a strong rival \Nin my designated area arrivals.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.87,0:17:32.33,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,Would that have been you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.33,0:17:34.32,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I'm not really sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.32,0:17:38.04,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Being in the same area doesn't \Nmean we're on the same table.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.39,0:17:43.71,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I thought you had no interest \Nin being in the top ten,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.99,0:17:46.27,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,but this morning, \Nyou were suddenly in 9th.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.56,0:17:55.21,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,This deserted island test \Nhas just been so much fun.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.59,0:17:58.81,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,I've found myself as excited as a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.14,0:18:02.81,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,I intend to keep going at \Nthis pace a bit longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.81,0:18:04.81,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,You're not aiming for number one?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.19,0:18:08.66,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,The top three slots are already \Nset up to be a bloodbath.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.98,0:18:15.32,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,Though I might reconsider if Nagumo \Nor Koenji starts to collapse.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.32,0:18:17.86,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Collapse?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.86,0:18:21.20,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,That seems very unlikely at the moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.52,0:18:24.97,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,You think Nagumo will just allow \NKoenji's dominance to stand?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.47,0:18:26.75,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,They could even end up
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.75,0:18:30.82,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,in a situation where they both \Nstruggle to acquire more game points.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.82,0:18:34.72,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Taking down rivals is also an \Nimportant part of the battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.96,0:18:37.35,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,You're not aiming for the top spots?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.35,0:18:41.60,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, it seems unlikely \Nthat I'll even crack the top ten.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.60,0:18:43.29,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.29,0:18:47.86,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,It seems to me you've been racking \Nup points at the same rate I have.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.31,0:18:51.55,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,A lot of groups will be losing \Nefficiency by this point.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.55,0:18:53.92,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,You just have to keep at it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.92,0:18:56.78,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,The bottom ten groups would \Nlove that, wouldn't they?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.78,0:19:00.37,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,They'd want to see any \Nother group drop out.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.62,0:19:05.46,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,When a person gets desperate, \Nthey become capable of anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.46,0:19:07.13,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,Don't let your guard down.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.47,0:19:11.88,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,As a girl, I think you're the one \Nwho should be worried about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.19,0:19:18.91,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,I suppose a beautiful maiden \Nsuch as myself should be more wary.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.39,0:19:24.64,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I meant it as a joke, but she seems \Nto be seriously considering it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.64,0:19:27.15,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,If it comes up, yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.37,0:19:30.40,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,I suppose I'll force my way through.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.40,0:19:33.90,Italics,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,That answer isn't maidenly at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.27,0:19:36.78,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,Sorry to take up your time.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.78,0:19:38.84,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,You're not going to the challenge?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.84,0:19:41.99,Main,Kiryuin,0,0,0,,You could probably still \Nregister if you hurry.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.99,0:19:43.98,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I don't think so.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.98,0:19:47.12,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I doubt I could beat the upperclassmen.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.14,0:20:02.19,Main,Shiranami,0,0,0,,Yume-chan?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.19,0:20:05.14,Main,Shiranami,0,0,0,,T-Takemoto-kun?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.56,0:20:06.91,Main,Shiranami,0,0,0,,Where are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.56,0:20:08.90,Main,Shiranami,0,0,0,,Yume-chan?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.15,0:20:12.90,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,No, I'm afraid I'm not Yume.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.11,0:20:16.90,Main,Shiranami,0,0,0,,Um, Ayanokoji-kun...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.12,0:20:18.42,Main,Shiranami,0,0,0,,Good evening.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.42,0:20:21.76,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Shiranami? Where are Kobashi and Takemoto?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.76,0:20:23.39,Main,Shiranami,0,0,0,,Um, well...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.80,0:20:27.92,Main,Shiranami,0,0,0,,I was rushing to keep up when \Nsuddenly I didn't know where I was...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.92,0:20:32.72,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Walking along aimlessly will \Njust get you more lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.72,0:20:34.42,Main,Shiranami,0,0,0,,R-Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.73,0:20:36.49,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Do you have stamina left?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.98,0:20:39.80,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Let's try to meet up with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.80,0:20:43.81,Main,Shiranami,0,0,0,,I do, but... how?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.81,0:20:49.49,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Use a GPS search and you can find \Ntheir general direction and distance.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.94,0:20:59.67,Main,Shiranami,0,0,0,,Why are you helping me?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.67,0:21:04.41,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,One element of this test is that \Nit's a battle between grade years.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.41,0:21:07.70,Main,Shiranami,0,0,0,,But you even used a GPS search...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.70,0:21:12.58,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,It's because you're in \NIchinose's class, I suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.92,0:21:17.59,Main,Shiranami,0,0,0,,Ayanokoji-kun, are you and Honami-chan...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.91,0:21:20.73,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,We're nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.73,0:21:22.68,Main,Kobashi,0,0,0,,Chihiro-chan!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.68,0:21:24.28,Main,Takemoto,0,0,0,,Shiranami!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.54,0:21:27.72,Main,Kobashi,0,0,0,,Chihiro-chan!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.42,0:21:29.92,Main,Takemoto,0,0,0,,Where are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.92,0:21:32.84,Main,Kobashi,0,0,0,,Chihiro-chan! Where are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.84,0:21:34.27,Main,Shiranami,0,0,0,,Yume-chan!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.86,0:21:37.40,Main,Shiranami,0,0,0,,Yume-chan!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.47,0:21:40.99,Main,Kobashi,0,0,0,,Chihiro-chan!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.99,0:21:42.11,Main,Kobashi,0,0,0,,Thank goodness!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.43,0:21:43.96,Main_Top,Kobashi,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.43,0:21:44.10,Main,Takemoto,0,0,0,,Thanks a lot, Ayanokoji.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.10,0:21:46.12,Main,Takemoto,0,0,0,,You really saved Shiranami back there.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.35,0:21:49.00,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,I do have a question for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.25,0:21:53.00,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Do you happen to have a transceiver?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.65,0:21:57.75,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,First...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.75,0:22:00.76,Main,Ayanokoji,0,0,0,,Sakayanagi, I'd like to ask you a favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.12,0:22:03.93,Italics,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,By all means, proceed.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.93,0:22:08.28,Italics,Sakayanagi,0,0,0,,I'll gladly return the favor \Nfor the classmates you helped.

